# THIS TARGET'S. The platform root has its own for the things every
# implementation would share (`__pycache__/`, `.venv`, `.env`); everything here
# is anchored to a directory only this target has.

# The agent under test, installed for `spike/probe_pi_cli.py`:
#
#     npm install --no-save @earendil-works/pi-coding-agent@0.85.1
#
# Not committed: 165 packages of someone else's bundle, pinned in the probe's own
# PINNED constant and in the Dockerfile, and the probe prints the version it
# actually measured so a mismatch is visible rather than assumed.
spike/node_modules/
spike/package-lock.json
spike/package.json

# Scratch space -- every probe workspace goes under here. Same "temp/*" +
# negation form the other implementations use: git never descends into a
# directory excluded by the bare directory form, so "!temp/.gitkeep" would
# silently never fire.
temp/*
!temp/.gitkeep
